<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Strada: Help</title>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_head.html.erb' %>
    <meta name="description" content="How to use Strada: connect Strava, view leaderboards and stats, configure sync, privacy, retention, timezone, units, fields, and maps for your Discord server."/>
    <meta property="og:title" content="Strada: Help">
    <meta property="og:description" content="How to use Strada: connect Strava, view leaderboards and stats, configure sync, privacy, retention, timezone, units, fields, and maps for your Discord server.">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Strada: Help">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="How to use Strada: connect Strava, view leaderboards and stats, configure sync, privacy, retention, timezone, units, fields, and maps for your Discord server.">
  </head>
  <body id="page-top" class="site-page help-page">
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_navigation.html.erb' %>
    <main id="main" class="page-container help-content">
      <header class="help-header">
        <h1>Strada: Help</h1>
        <p>Connect Strava, share activities, and manage your Discord channel.</p>
      </header>
      <section id="get-started" class="help-section">
        <h2>Get started</h2>
        <p>You'll need a Discord server and a Strava account. <a href="https://www.strava.com/register">Sign up for Strava</a> if you need one.</p>
        <ol class="getting-started-steps">
          <li><a href="https://discord.com/api/oauth2/authorize?scope=identify+bot&client_id=<%= ENV['DISCORD_CLIENT_ID'] %>&permissions=2147502080&redirect_uri=<%= ENV['URL'] %>&response_type=code">Add Strada to Discord</a> and choose your server. You may need a server administrator's permission.</li>
          <li>In your activity channel, run <code>/strada help</code> to check that the bot responds.</li>
          <li>Run <code>/strada connect</code> and follow the link to sign in and authorize Strava outside Discord.</li>
          <li>Save a new Strava activity after connecting. Its notification will appear in that channel.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="help-note">To stop sharing, use <code>/strada disconnect</code>.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="commands" class="help-section">
        <h2>Commands and settings</h2>
        <p>Send commands in the Discord channel where Strada is installed. Choose a topic for examples.</p>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Leaderboards and statistics</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>/strada leaderboard</code></dt>
            <dd>Show the channel's distance leaderboard. Choose a metric with <code>/strada leaderboard distance</code>, <code>/strada leaderboard time</code>, or <code>/strada leaderboard count</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada stats</code></dt>
            <dd>Show aggregate activity statistics for the past 30 days.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada leaderboard last week</code></dt>
            <dd>Choose a time range, such as <code>elapsed time last month</code>, <code>since 2024</code>, or <code>between January and March</code>. Longer ranges may require increasing retention below.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Sharing and privacy</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>/strada set sync false</code></dt>
            <dd>Pause activity sharing. Resume with <code>/strada set sync true</code> (the default).</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set private true</code></dt>
            <dd>Include private activities. They are hidden by default; restore that setting with <code>/strada set private false</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set followers false</code></dt>
            <dd>Hide followers-only activities. They are included by default; restore with <code>/strada set followers true</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada disconnect</code></dt>
            <dd>Unlink your Strava account. To disconnect another member, use <code>/strada disconnect @mention</code>.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Units, maps, and fields</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>/strada set units metric</code></dt>
            <dd>Use kilometers, meters, and Celsius. Choose <code>imperial</code> for miles, feet, yards, and Fahrenheit (the default), or <code>both</code> to display both sets.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set maps thumb</code></dt>
            <dd>Use map thumbnails. Choose <code>off</code> to hide maps or <code>full</code> for full maps (the default).</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set fields</code></dt>
            <dd>Choose displayed fields with <code>default</code>, <code>all</code>, or <code>none</code>. Available fields: <%= ActivityFields.values.and { |v| '<code>' + v + '</code>' } %>.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Retention, timezone, and posting limits</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>/strada set retention 60 days</code></dt>
            <dd>Discord server admins can change the default 30-day retention. Durations such as <code>3 months</code> also work.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set timezone Pacific Time (US &amp; Canada)</code></dt>
            <dd>Choose the timezone for date ranges and daily limits, or use <code>auto</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set userlimit 5</code></dt>
            <dd>Limit each user's daily activity posts. Use <code>/strada set userlimit none</code> to remove the limit.</dd>
            <dt><code>/strada set channellimit 10</code></dt>
            <dd>Limit daily posts across the channel. Use <code>/strada set channellimit none</code> to remove the limit.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section id="support" class="help-section">
        <h2>Contact support</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:dblock@vestris.com">dblock@vestris.com</a> with the command, channel type, approximate time and time zone, and any error message. Don't send passwords or access tokens.</p>
      </section>
      <p class="affiliation-note">Powered by Strava; not officially affiliated with <a href="https://www.nyrr.org/">NYRR</a> or <a href="https://www.strava.com">Strava</a>.</p>
    </main>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_footer.html.erb' %>
  </body>
</html>
